---
title: Groundnut Stew
source: Green Roasting Tin
tags: vegan
servings: 4
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 1 hour
---

Preheat the oven to 180°C.

Mix @sweet potatoes{1%kg}(peeled and cut into 1cm slices), @onion{1}(roughly sliced), @ginger{2.5%cm}(grated), @garlic{2%clove}(crushed), and @Scotch bonnet chilli{1}(pierced) with @olive oil{1%tbsp} and @sea salt{1%tsp} in a #roasting tin{}.

Transfer to the oven and cook for ~{45%minutes}, until the sweet potato is just soft when prodded with a fork.

Mix together @peanut butter{50%g}, @tomatoes{}(chopped), and @vegetable stock{400%ml}, and pour over the roasted sweet potatoes. Give everything a good stir, then return to the oven for a further ~{15%minutes}.

Fish out the Scotch bonnet, season to taste with @sea salt{}, and scatter over the @coriander{}(chopped) and @salted peanuts{}(roughly chopped). Serve with hot @white rice{}.
